  "id": "avar_folk_song",
  "name": "Avar song (Dagestan highland song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song tradition of the Avars, the largest people of Dagestan, centred on the highland Khunzakh plateau. Lyrical and heroic songs are sung by a solo voice to the bowed chagana spike fiddle, represented here by the neighbouring Ossetian kissyn-fandyr card, and the plucked pandur and tamur lutes, represented by the Nakh phandyr card; outdoor wedding and dance music on zurna and double-headed drum is part of the wider tradition but is left out of this song default. It is documented in Melodiya's Dagestan folk series and the Makhachkala Radio archive.",
  "recipe": "classic modern avar song, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. melodic bowed song accompaniment kissyn fandyr, phandyr. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
